diff --git a/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/10_TELEMETRY_PIPELINE.md b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/10_TELEMETRY_PIPELINE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d331059
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/10_TELEMETRY_PIPELINE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,85 @@
+# Courier Fair Pay — Telemetry Pipeline V0.1
+
+## Rule
+
+Apps and operational services emit factual events. They do not calculate wages.
+
+Flow:
+
+`Client / Merchant / Courier / API / OPS / Payments events`
+→ `raw clock + money telemetry`
+→ `strict normalizer`
+→ `canonical payroll facts`
+→ `weekly projector`
+→ `Fair Pay Kernel`
+→ `weekly statement`
+
+## Existing signals found in the current codebase
+
+AVAILABLE:
+- mission/order acceptance: `acceptedAt`;
+- merchant/order ready state: `readyAt` / status `ready`;
+- pickup: `pickedUpAt`;
+- delivery: `deliveredAt`.
+
+PARTIAL:
+- tips/payment domain exists, but no canonical Courier payroll fact mapping is established.
+
+MISSING / must be explicit:
+- `courierArrivedPickupAt`;
+- required reposition start/end;
+- other paid work start/end;
+- legally validated eligible-income credit;
+- expense reimbursement credit.
+
+## Why pickup arrival is mandatory
+
+`acceptedAt`, `readyAt` and `pickedUpAt` do not prove when the courier reached the merchant.
+
+Therefore the kernel must not infer restaurant waiting from those timestamps.
+
+No `PICKUP_ARRIVED` event → no normalized mission time facts for payroll finalization.
+
+## Normalized mission clock
+
+When all four clock signals exist:
+
+`MISSION_ACCEPTED → PICKUP_ARRIVED`
+= ACTIVE_MISSION
+
+`PICKUP_ARRIVED → PICKED_UP`
+= PLATFORM_CONTROLLED_WAITING / pickup dwell
+
+`PICKED_UP → DELIVERED`
+= ACTIVE_MISSION
+
+The merchant-ready event is retained as an operational diagnostic. It does not independently create or erase worker entitlement.
+
+## France-specific duration
+
+The French activity guarantee uses a separate `ACTIVITY_GUARANTEE_ESTIMATE` duration fact.
+
+It is not derived from actual mission timestamps.
+
+If a country policy requires an activity guarantee and the explicit estimate is absent, calculation fails with:
+
+`COURIER_PAYROLL_ACTIVITY_GUARANTEE_DURATION_REQUIRED`
+
+## OPS segments
+
+Required repositioning and other paid work are normalized only from explicit START/END pairs sharing a segment ID.
+
+Missing end/start → segment remains incomplete and cannot silently enter payroll.
+
+## Audit
+
+Every normalized fact contains:
+- stable fact ID;
+- policy ID;
+- country;
+- courier;
+- week;
+- raw evidence event IDs;
+- source = `PAYROLL_NORMALIZER`.
+
+This lets every statement amount be traced back to factual events.
diff --git a/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/11_POLICY_LEDGER_AND_STATEMENT.md b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/11_POLICY_LEDGER_AND_STATEMENT.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3df004c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/11_POLICY_LEDGER_AND_STATEMENT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
+# Policy Ledger & Weekly Statement V0.1
+
+## Immutable policy principle
+
+Every country/status policy is sealed with SHA-256 over canonical JSON.
+
+Snapshot 27 October 2026:
+
+- Belgium `BE-EMPLOYEE-POG-FAIR-PAY-LAB-v0.1`
+  - hash: `5f0ca2b5349dee3921aede627b0519355d32857df5624866ce7e26b53cdb229c`
+  - validation: DRAFT
+  - production: blocked
+
+- France `FR-INDEPENDENT-ARPE-2026-09-01-v1`
+  - hash: `ae0794c9fb2d0408c545ff0fb58293bfe2a4fdc7147741f19429872cdbf44d4a`
+  - validation: LEGAL_REVIEW
+  - production: blocked
+
+A policy cannot be modified under the same `policyId` without triggering an integrity error.
+
+A changed rule requires a new version.
+
+## Weekly statement
+
+Statement identity is deterministic from:
+- policy hash;
+- sorted source facts;
+- calculation result;
+- statement version.
+
+Example Belgium statement:
+- statement ID: `9c6c574d92fdbde7ba3a53033a48a035aba209463c8bff3c960e875c9a44cb63`
+- facts hash: `5c7bd1b727c32c999520e2ee19b885f898072a80fa89e9560c7ee56924695cac`
+- paid time: 5,400 seconds = 90 min;
+- active mission: 3,000 seconds = 50 min;
+- pickup waiting/dwell: 600 seconds = 10 min;
+- required reposition: 900 seconds = 15 min;
+- other paid work: 900 seconds = 15 min;
+- eligible income: 26.00 EUR;
+- POG LAB floor: 28.50 EUR;
+- true-up: 2.50 EUR;
+- tips: 5.00 EUR;
+- expenses: 3.00 EUR;
+- total cash due: 36.50 EUR.
+
+Warnings are preserved in the statement:
+- country policy not legally GREEN;
+- legal floor not configured;
+- low utilization belongs to POG zone risk.
+
+## Contestability
+
+The statement contract is explicitly `contestable: true`.
+
+Future production implementation must add:
+- visible explanation;
+- support/dispute entry point;
+- human correction workflow;
+- immutable correction trail;
+- settlement state/payment reference.
diff --git a/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/12_BELGIUM_SENSITIVITY_FINDINGS.md b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/12_BELGIUM_SENSITIVITY_FINDINGS.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..08b2769
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/12_BELGIUM_SENSITIVITY_FINDINGS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,71 @@
+# Belgium Sensitivity Findings — LAB
+
+All numbers in this file are laboratory assumptions, not approved production economics.
+
+## Economic sweep
+
+Variables swept:
+- employer courier cost: 26–34 EUR / paid hour;
+- contribution available before Courier: 9–14 EUR / delivery;
+- target residual contribution: 2 EUR / delivery.
+
+At 30 EUR employer cost per paid hour:
+
+| Contribution before Courier | Break-even deliveries/h | Deliveries/h for 2 EUR residual/order |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 9 EUR | 3.33 | 4.29 |
+| 10 EUR | 3.00 | 3.75 |
+| 11 EUR | 2.73 | 3.33 |
+| 12 EUR | 2.50 | 3.00 |
+| 13 EUR | 2.31 | 2.73 |
+| 14 EUR | 2.14 | 2.50 |
+
+The implication is structural: contribution per order and delivery density are coupled. There is no single universal viable density.
+
+## Waiting-time sensitivity
+
+Illustrative operational assumption:
+- 17 min base travel/handling per delivery;
+- employer cost 30 EUR/h;
+- contribution before Courier 12 EUR/delivery.
+
+Without batching:
+
+| Merchant wait/order | Deliveries/h | Residual/h |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 0 min | 3.53 | +12.35 EUR |
+| 3 min | 3.00 | +6.00 EUR |
+| 6 min | 2.61 | +1.30 EUR |
+| 9 min | 2.31 | -2.31 EUR |
+| 12 min | 2.07 | -5.17 EUR |
+
+With a LAB batch-efficiency multiplier of 1.20:
+
+| Merchant wait/order | Deliveries/h | Residual/h |
+| ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| 0 min | 4.24 | +20.82 EUR |
+| 3 min | 3.60 | +13.20 EUR |
+| 6 min | 3.13 | +7.57 EUR |
+| 9 min | 2.77 | +3.23 EUR |
+| 12 min | 2.48 | -0.21 EUR |
+
+## Interpretation
+
+Merchant waiting can erase the economics of a fair-pay fleet even when courier pay itself is correctly designed.
+
+Therefore Merchant readiness is not merely UX. It is part of Payroll viability.
+
+Batching can recover capacity, but it must never be treated as permission to overload or create unsafe route pressure.
+
+## Required pilot measurements
+
+Before accepting these laboratory thresholds:
+- actual employer cost;
+- actual contribution before Courier;
+- real merchant wait distribution;
+- actual non-wait cycle time;
+- achievable safe batching;
+- cancellation/incident effect;
+- demand profile by 15/30-minute interval.
+
+The simulator must be recalibrated with observed pilot data.
diff --git a/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/13_MASTER_TODO.md b/docs/courier-fair-pay-lab/13_MASTER_TODO.md
